hi it's michelle from lab muffin beauty  science chemistry phd skincare nerd and  a bit of a mess i don't know about you  but over the last year with lockdowns  and working from home and general stress  my daily routine has just gone out the  window i keep losing track  of when i last changed my sheets when i  should be eating lunch when i should go  to sleep  some days i've even forgotten to shower  until it's too late for me to shower  so a lot of nights i just haven't had  the energy to do a proper full skincare  routine  it's sort of like the last thing on my  mind and with mask wearing my skin has  needed more attention  i'm getting a lot of congestion around  my chin and i might be starting to  develop a little bit of perioral  dermatitis  so today i thought i'd talk about some  skin care products that i found really  helpful  when i've just been too lazy to do a  proper routine or when i have to play  catch-up with my skincare let me know  what products you like using for this if  you use the same products as me  if you like talking about the science  behind beauty products click the like  the subscribe and the notification bell  so you don't miss any videos  i'm going to start with today's video  sponsor and it's a product that i think  a lot of you knew i was going to talk  about for this which is  bioderma's micellar water i talk about  this a lot but analyzing an ingredients  list is useful to an extent  but because products are so complex you  can't tell everything just from the  ingredients list  that's why testing products on actual  people getting clinical evidence  is so valuable in getting science-based  skin care  and that's why so many skin care experts  scientists dermatologists  estheticians recommend bioderma all the  time they are so  thorough with their clinical testing  they collaborate with research  institutes and dermatologists to create  their products  and that means they end up with products  that just work really well  for a lot of people i've raved about  their micellar water before and it's  become such a staple for me over the  last year  this is actually the world's first  micellar water it's the product that  started the craze  it's a really gentle cleanser that's  effective at removing dirt oil makeup  and pollution  without disrupting the skin's barrier  very much and so that makes it really  good for sensitive skin  in clinical testing 97 of people with  fragile or sensitive skin  found they had a soothing effect from  this cleanser i've talked to so many  dermatologists and makeup  artists and people with sensitive skin  who also rave about this  now not all micellar waters are  formulated for sensitive skin but this  one has a number of features that makes  it really good  it has a skin friendly ph of 5.5 and  it's fragrance free and it contains  one single gentle surfactant now i know  we tend to think of surfactants as  harsh irritating ingredients but it's  actually a really broad category  unlike a lot of rinse-off cleanses and  other micellar waters on the market  this only has one super gentle non-ionic  surfactant ingredient  it's a skin softening amole moisturizer  that can actually counteract irritation  the water they use is also special it's  highly purified injection quality water  and in a lot of other cosmetic products  the water has endotoxins which  for most people is okay but if you have  very sensitive skin  it can be irritating i love this  cleanser you can use it as the first  step of a double cleansing routine  or i usually use it as a standalone  cleanser i use it with reusable cotton  pairs  mine are from bamboo face and i found  that these are really gentle  i used to use it with cheap cotton pads  and i found that my skin was getting a  bit sensitive and that was actually  because the cotton pad was rough  once i switched to a softer pad i found  that i didn't have issues so it was just  the physical exfoliation from the cotton  pad  so if i have makeup on i'll probably use  two cotton pads if i don't have makeup  i'll just use  one and then wipe it all over my face  then chuck this into the laundry  it also used to be my travel cleanser  back when we were actually traveling  i've also started using this in the  morning just as a morning cleanse  if you know my skincare routine i used  to just splash my face with water  and then pat it off because my skin's  really dehydration prone  but my skin's changed so much from  wearing masks after seeing a derma  clinician which is what we call  estheticians in australia she suggested  that maybe  i should cleanse my face in the morning  as well maybe that one cleanse in the  evening wasn't quite enough  so i've just started doing this i'll  keep you updated on how that goes  so apart from the micellar water which i  think is my one big  love from bioderma they have lots of  other great products i feel like  everyone in my family is now using at  least one bioderma product  another of my favorites is the sebum  foaming gel cleanser which is what i use  a lot of the time when i do a proper  cleanse  i've reviewed the sebum rage before it  contains a bunch of actives that  really help with pimples without drying  out your skin  so it helps with poor clogging and oil  and the whole range works really well  alongside traditional  acne treatments i also love the autoderm  range especially in winter it's great  for dry skin it's really good for  strengthening your barrier  and restoring lipids the next product  i'm talking about is kate somerville's  xfolicade  this is a rinse off exfoliating product  i guess you could call it a peel  or a mask you're meant to leave it on  for about two minutes  and this is my catcher product for when  i've forgotten to exfoliate  i use this a lot in the shower and  because it's rinse off it fits in really  easily with the rest of my routine  i don't have to worry about whether or  not it's going to interact with  something else or peel up  this is a chemical and physical and  enzyme exfoliant so it's got alpha  hydroxy acid it's got lactic acid  bha which is salicylic acid it has tiny  silica scrubbing granules so you  apply it by massaging it on for about 30  seconds  and then you'd leave it on after that  for you're meant to leave it on for a  total of two minutes i'm sure i've left  it on for longer without problems  there's also three types of enzymes in  this it's got papaya pumpkin and  pineapple enzymes  so it's basically ticked off every  exfoliation category i regularly use  apart from maybe  peeling gel and phase now this is a bit  expensive it's a bit more bougie than  i normally go for but it lasts for ages  so  i only use about a pencil a race's worth  every time and i think in total  i think i'm on my second tube they also  recently launched a 15 mil version which  is a bit more affordable so it's great  if you're not sure if you want to commit  to  a proper tube yet i've tried some other  peel products  but i always end up going back to this  because it works really well  it has all three types of exfoliants but  it also just has a really great texture  it's a thick green paste and it stays on  your skin really well  it doesn't drip down your face when  you're in the shower with all the steam  a lot of other peel products are very  liquid and very runny so  when i'm in the shower i can feel it  dripping down my face this one does not  so i am still paranoid enough to keep it  above my eyebrows but  yeah i haven't really felt this running  into my eyes yet and i still have my  eyes  next i have the paula's choice point  three percent rational and two percent  pecutial treatment  i really like this because it has this  combination bucutial is a plant extract  that helps with wrinkles and  hyperpigmentation  and it's been marketed as like an  alternative to retinol  it really isn't it's not a retinoid it  doesn't work the same way  even though it has a similar overall  effect but  so do a lot of other ingredients in skin  care but it is still a pretty promising  ingredient  now according to paula's choice the  pecutial can help the retinal work more  effectively  i don't know what evidence they have for  this i tried looking through their  references but they have a really awful  referencing system so i can't tell what  paper they're talking about  anyway this is a really nice light  lotion apart from the retinol ambicucial  there's also peptides and skin soothing  ingredients  and so that means we have a rational  product that isn't all that irritating  which means you don't have to be that  careful with the application  some nights i'm just too tired to  carefully measure out a tiny bit of  tretinoin i can't trust myself with that  responsibility  because it's got that combination of  ingredients i don't feel like i need to  use  extra products and because my skin is  more on the oily side this works as my  moisturizer as well  if your skin is a bit drier then maybe  that won't work you might need an extra  product  along the same lines this is kate ryan's  total nutrition night repair complex  i've raved about this product before  it's a very similar idea it's an  all-in-one product that just makes your  skin look really nice the next day  it has a bit of everything it's got  niacinamide retinol acetate  centella extract and antioxidants so  this is really great for when i want my  skin to look a bit  nicer but i also don't want to risk any  sort of irritation so  the night before filming a video now on  nights when i feel a bit more capable of  using trash i  really love the claire's midnight blue  calming cream  this is really good for mixing with  tretinoin and it calms the skin down a  bit so if i go a little bit  overboard on the trash then i'm a bit  safer  and it also helps the tretinoin spread  over skin much faster so i just mix it  on the palm of my hand with  about a half pea-sized amount of treason  on and then spread it all over  i've also been enjoying glow recipes lip  pop so there are skin care brand that  have  recently branched out and they've  launched lip products and body products  they have a lot of fruit branding so  this smells delicious it smells like  watermelon  it's a really rich soft moisturizing lip  balm and it also doubles up as a lip  scrub  it's got little sugar granules in it  that dissolve over time  and alpha hydroxy acids and so i use  this at night  it also has a little bit of a stain in  it i have the sort of coloring where i  look a little bit dead if i don't have  some sort of color on my face especially  on the lips  and so wearing this at night means that  when i wake up in the morning my lips  are already  sort of a little bit made up and so if i  just wake up  five minutes before a zoom call i don't  look too bad  i hope you like the video if you have  any other product suggestions for me to  incorporate into my  lazy skincare toolkit let me know you  can give it a thumbs up  and subscribe for more videos like this  you can also follow me on instagram and  check out my blog for more of the  science behind beauty products  see you next time to nerd out more

